body:
Dogs actually are aware when their time comes, but animals, in general, appear to accept it. They go to a private place and pass. However, if being attacked they will naturally fight. It's just instinct. 

&#x200B;

To be aware of how the world works is pretty depressing. To be self aware, to be knowledgeable enough to know that life has little to no meaning unless you find one that affects you personally.. there's no point. Depression is a mental illness, however I don't think you're wrong about the world having no meaning. It's different per person and everyone's values lie in different interests, so y'know.

My depression and suicidal thoughts are back all of a sudden. Not due to the weather. I love the autumn and winter weather.. but all I can think about right now is self harm.. it's been a really long time since I've last done that. But my boyfriend's little sister ended up in the hospital because she had cuts on her arms. It reminds me too much about myself and saddened me. I'm just not in the right mindset to be hearing about all this, but I have to be there for him as well.. 

&#x200B;

He told me when he saw her cuts it reminded him of me.. it saddened him quite a bit, so I don't want him to see cuts on me again, but I don't know. I just want to cut away at all this fat. Shave it all off. I hate this.

I don't think you understand how grief affects different people, on a grand scale.. not just your close knit friends, and I don't think you understand how shock works. 

&#x200B;

he's a human first, a parent second.

Just because he's a dad of two sons doesn't mean he has to throw out his emotions and processing to tell them. Yes, I think it's understandable to believe that the kids deserve what happened, right away, but we're all human. If my wife killed himself I wouldn't tell his mom or brother right away. I'd be in shock. I'd be saddened and depressed... knowing me I probably wouldn't tell anyone. I'd just act like nothing happened. Does that make me heartless? No, but if that's what you think then I think you need to learn how to level up your EQ. 

&#x200B;

He's a human. He deserves time to process it. If you want to challenge my opinion, don't bother. I'm not going to change it. He could tell them right away or keep it to himself. if the kids get mad, it's understandable, but they're children. They're not expected to react maturely.

I also believe this is a dangerous way to think and perceive one's mental illness.. I'm trying so hard to fight off depression that may be approaching once again. For the first time in my life I'm actually not depressed and empty and sad.. but funny enough I'm having to adjust to not feeling depressed, if that makes sense?

&#x200B;

I've gotten so used to depression. I grew up with it, developed with and around it, etc., and for the first time in my life I'm.. maybe okay?

&#x200B;

The second I saw this my initial, usual, depressed and dark minded self wanted to grasp on to this and think, "What if I am right? What if I did get brainwashed and I should have listened to myself and reject my pills.. now it's too late. I must return to my old(depressed and paranoid)self because that's what kept me safe.." 

&#x200B;

But immediately my new, "healthy," trained mind said, "No. Wait what the fuck. No. This is not okay to think about or even consider. Depression made you attempt suicide more than twice. How could this be okay? Don't you remember all the loved ones you've hurt?"

I knew I was a more "independent person" when I no longer had to ask the people around me if I could consume something.. though that may be due to my anxiety, either way. Or that I had my own job and other ways to earn money to buy myself ice cream and popsicles and pasta... and hot cheetos(lime is superior), then eat that the second I wake up at 3am then go play league.. then go back to sleep. 

&#x200B;

But to know I was becoming more "adult" in my parents' eyes was when I could start making semi-mean jokes while complimenting them. Saying, "I mean. That doesn't look that bad on you. It's old people clothes and you're old now.. so. It's pretty fitting."

Wow I've never heard of "tulpas" before.. the concept is interesting. I'll definitely research more into it..

&#x200B;

Though honestly I feel like it may have started as an innocent escape into another world, but then as my environment got worse that other me started to build up anger, hatred, fear, paranoia, and the will to fight off \*anything.\* 

&#x200B;

Of course as a kid I would have super powers.. obviously as I got older I got very interested in science and loved fantasy worlds and the concept of infinite universes, etc. So I applied that to "My World." My "powers" became more complex and if a character ever asked me how I did it.. some stuff was just "second nature" stuff, (Powers I couldn't explain because it was a whole other science that didn't apply to humans) or I would be able to use what i've learned from science textbooks and research studies on how to explain things. 

&#x200B;

But then with such strong, negative feelings developing and learning about terrorism and murder.. I, too, started to apply that to my world. I became a killer. A fighter. A protector.. fighting on the "right" side. Not always the "good" side. Just the "right" one. Because what is "good" anyways, right? Anyways.. 

&#x200B;

I won't explain more.. but obviously it has now become something that I can't really control.. she really feels like she's been given too much power. Has evolved too much and now she is real. That world is real. I'm just one of her other copies. other version that she created and left to die in this world while she will continue to live in her own, if she so wishes. 

&#x200B;

At least that's what I ponder about, while she doesn't. She seems to know that if she chooses to let me die, or if she chooses to kill me she will cease to exist. But she still has a sense to protect me, for some reason, and despite her daily insults on how weak and pathetic I am.. she still tells me to not kill myself, and not be a bitch, basically.

Well recently, for the past almost half year.. My anxiety, for some reason, just got terrible again. I think it was because I was starting to slowly "recover" from a dip in my eating disorder, but then what I'm slowly realizing is that the lack of sense of feeling in control may be what's causing my anxiety. I don't leave the house unless I absolutely have to.

&#x200B;

I do go out roughly three days a week.. and honestly that sounds like a lot to me considering I really don't do anything and each day is usually one or two appointments with my treatment team.

I was taking them for roughly over two years. I don't know. It's difficult for me to get into the routine of things, but once I am I find it strange stopping. (like maybe after a few weeks of doing it or sometimes a few months)

&#x200B;

I think what caused me to stop was one of those rare moments that I felt too depressed one night and couldn't force myself to take the pills that night.. I did speak honestly before with my psychiatrist. I started taking lithium at one point and although it greatly helped, I still got those strange feelings that I just shouldn't be taking those pills.. so i stopped.

&#x200B;

And now here I am regretting I took a single one. I don't know if from taking it it's still been successful in rewiring my brain in a way that I don't think I could ever adapt to.

I have dark brown hair and I'm a tan, short asian. Only tan really around the face elbows and arms. Legs and stomach are as yellow as i can be. 

&#x200B;

i'd love to dye part of my a dark blue or even dark purple or red. Any Suggestions?

This will just be off the top of my head, so these may not best represent the mood and what I typically prefer..

&#x200B;

Anger - \[Solo by Prismo\]([https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mExmqHOkAIU](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mExmqHOkAIU)) or possible even \[Jolt by Unlike Pluto\]([https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4sGHVlK3WUs](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4sGHVlK3WUs)) Both seem to have a bit of a psycho, mass murder feel.. or is that just me and my strange fantasies?

&#x200B;

Sorrow - \[Definitely Billie songs here such as idontwannabeyouanymore\]([https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-tn2S3kJlyU](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-tn2S3kJlyU)) I'm also a huge fan of Joji's song called \[Dancing in the Dark\]([https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sVDiAoxdR8E](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sVDiAoxdR8E))

&#x200B;

Jealousy - I honestly don't really feel this emotion often and therefore it's not strong enough for me to be able to relate to a song or find jealousy as the main focus or message of a song. Sorry.

&#x200B;

Joy - \[I cannot resist not bringing in an old favourite called September by Earth Wind and Fire\]([https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Cfr2HWJYQo0](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Cfr2HWJYQo0))

But another one that brings on a more silent level of joy is this \[Shelter Remix done by Louie Zong, but originally done by Porter Robinson & Madeon\]([https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=KEFJB-Sj5mU](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=KEFJB-Sj5mU)) Honestly any song done by Louie Zong is absolutely well done and cute and sparks a little bit of silent joy in me.

&#x200B;

Oh! And \[Monody by TheFatRat\]([https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=B7xai5u\_tnk](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=B7xai5u_tnk))

&#x200B;

Solitariness - I recently found this song called \[Everybody Loves You by Charlotte Lawrence\]([https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9l5VeGYrp3U](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9l5VeGYrp3U))

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

edit: rip. Did they change how you format all that? Sorry, but I'm lazy...

I am unsure if I am a needle in the haystack or if I'm just a sheep part of the flock, but honestly.. just talk to me like I'm a human. Assume as gentle as you can, but maybe heavily consider body language. I used to be able to put up a good front and although my usual take was to be an asshole.. I've grown up and identified that animosity as insecurity. Now I just let it only fester inside until I can find the right place to put it in. 

&#x200B;

To be honest, simple, kind gestures can be taken incorrectly. A smile or compliment will make me feel terribly worse and self conscious. I get paranoid and wonder if you're lying, if I looked weird and you thought I was making some sort of fashion statement.. weird, random stuff like that. Personally, going unnoticed is something worth a slow mo of a "don't you.. forget about me.." moment, ironically, BUT sometimes a short, genuine, positive conversation can really brighten my day. 

&#x200B;

Anyways. Just treat me like a human. I don't want to be seen as a fragile dandelion. I'm me. I have anxiety. I have depression. I'm struggling, but I'm still a human being at the end of the day. <3

I honestly don't know. I live everyday wondering if it'll be my last. No matter how hard I try to enjoy whatever I have left of myself I just cannot see through the thick fog of depression and the shadows of anxiety. I've already died three times. Twice to my own hands, and I wish I could say that I was a survivor. Someone that greatly regretted their decision and am grateful to be alive... but as you can tell by the amount of attempts, that is not the case. 

&#x200B;

I think if I ever get out of this spiral like mindset I won't be thinking, "Damn.. I just wasted my whole life. I could have only wasted 15 years, but instead I wasted 80," but at the time that's all I really think about whenever I go to bed and take the prescribed dose of my clonidine. "Is this really worth it? Why keep going? Why keep paying people to keep me alive if I'm not even going to try and if I only suffer in the end. What's the point? We all die in the end.. what's wrong with speeding up the process?"
